  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Derived-data cache: routing cards, claim verification, and validation reports are cached process-wide, keyed by (path, size, mtime) fingerprints of every file each computation consulted — bundle documents, cited sources, and link targets. Repeated MCP calls re-stat instead of re-reading and re-hashing, and one verification pass reads each cited source file once however many claims cite it.\n- Leaner reads: read_component returns document bodies by default; claims arrive structurally, now including claims whose citation no longer verifies, flagged citationBroken instead of hidden. A verbatim read returns exact file text for editing and merges. The response budget is 64 KiB, and a single oversized document is truncated and flagged instead of failing the read.\n- prepare_okf_fill points at okf_authoring_guide instead of inlining three of its sections into every fill.\n- Agent integration: init generates the octoevidence workflow skill (SKILL.md standard) for detected Claude Code and Codex installs, and wires a Claude Code Stop hook. The new `octoevidence hook stop` blocks session handoff with actionable feedback while OKF validation fails, and warns without blocking on unreconciled drift.",
